Parent: 1444

## Context
Author clarification, 2026-11-07: first diagnose whether script-calling instructions recover from unavailable helpers. Transcript absence may reflect unavailable environments and cannot establish that a fallback works. No universal manual-route rewrite is commissioned.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Harness-doctor retains an on-demand reading diagnostic for missing, unavailable, and failing helper paths in a bounded set of script-calling instructions; inputs, decisions, checks, outputs, authorization, and verification are assessed.
- [ ] A known recovery gap and an adequate route serve as controls; source locations and unexamined behavior are explicit. Transcript evidence is supplementary, not required to infer availability from silence.
- [ ] A manual route is added only where the diagnostic establishes a concrete gap; otherwise report the bounded result and evidence limits. No blanket workflow rewrite.
- [ ] No new general rule, routine healthcheck, scheduled sweep, merge gate, or prose-wording test.
